      "dom_id": "question-326465",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "According to a recent report, $60%$ of tablet owners said they used their tablets regularly. Of those, $50%$ said they used them primarily for drawing. What percentage of all tablet owners used tablets primarily for drawing?",
      "worked_solution": "Let $x$ be the total number of tablet owners.\n\nWe're told that $60%$ of tablet owners used their tablets regularly. Thus, the number of tablet owners who use them regularly is $0.6x.$\n\nWe are also told that of those owners, $50%$ used them for drawing. So, the number of tablet owners who used tablets primarily for drawing is\n\n$$\n0.50(0.6x)=0.30x.\n$$\n\nThe expression $0.30x$ represents $30%$ of $x.$ Therefore, $30%$ of all tablet owners used tablets primarily for drawing.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [],
