      "problem": "An event organizer raised a ticket’s price to $160%$ of its original cost. A tax of $10%$ was applied to the marked-up price. If the ticket originally cost $$75,$ what is the tax?\n\nThe tax on the ticket is $$$  \n{{field-1}}.",
      "worked_solution": "First, the marked-up price is $160%$ of the original cost $($75):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}160%\\times 75 & =\\frac{160}{100}\\times 75 \\\\  & =1.6\\times 75 \\\\  & =120\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the marked-up price of the ticket is $$120.$ Then, the tax is $10%$ of this price:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}10%\\times 120 & =\\frac{10}{100}\\times 120 \\\\  & =0.1\\times 120 \\\\  & =12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the tax on the ticket is $$12.$",
